# Root schema shared by all modules.
#
# Two kinds of comments exist in GraphQL:
#   - "# like this" is only for people reading the file;
#   - """like this""" (a description) becomes part of the API and is shown in
#     the Playground's Docs panel and to any client using introspection.
#
# After changing any .graphqls file, run `make graphql` to regenerate Go code.

"""
Rejects the field unless the caller's access token carries the permission.
Implemented by hasPermission in internal/graph/handler.go.
"""
directive @hasPermission(permission: String!) on FIELD_DEFINITION

"""
An RFC 3339 timestamp, e.g. "2026-10-09T20:16:22+05:00". Built into gqlgen
and mapped to Go's time.Time.
"""
scalar Time

# The root types are declared empty here. Each module adds its fields with
# `extend type Query` / `extend type Mutation` in its own file, so modules
# stay independent.

"Read-only operations."
type Query

"Operations that change data."
type Mutation
